 r←OnHeader msg
⍝ Note that you can access the server data (configuration, INI instance etc.) via the reference `G` (for "Globals").
 ⎕←'OnHeader...'
 r←0
 :If '/crash-in-header'≡⎕C msg.Path
     ⎕←'Client asked for a crash in OnHeader'
     ∘∘∘ ⍝ In runtime this will be caught by Rumba's "TrapRequest" operator which then attempts to send back a 500
 :EndIf
 :If 0<#.⎕NC'TEMP'
     #.TEMP.Log,←⊂'Header'
 :EndIf
⍝Done
